WEBVTT

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.550
There is a colossal creation of a common imagination.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.000
This whole story is a folk legend.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.890
and tell it in almost the same simplicity as Gogol heard.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:16.570
So, going home, it's a pity not to fix the road, because on the last vacations, two bursars, having been poisoned by demons, stole a hen, a litter of acorns and a lemish, and a bass.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:29.950
Three others, having sold the Hodorov deacon, forced him to sing unnecessary songs. Disgrace! Let's pray to God!

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:40.500
Spirit of wisdom and reason, send me, Lord!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:51.180
And enlighten my heart and mind!

00:03:51.180 --> 00:04:00.000
For there is a punishment and a punishment!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.800
And all your glory be learned, Amen!

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.950
And all your glory be learned, Amen!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.360
Amen!

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.560
To the Republic of the Most Holy Mother of God,

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:19.560
all be in the bursar!

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.000
Hooray!

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.000
What the hell? I thought it was going to be a farm.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.160
God damn it, I can't see a damn fist.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:19.110
- Where's the road? - There's no road.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.330
You go to the right, and I'll look for it straight.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.360
And the raven... The raven...

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:40.160
Damn, I got you mixed up with a stump.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.620
- What's there? - There's no road, only fox holes.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:05.180
- You'll hear it at home. - Sit down!

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.630
So, shall we stay and spend the night in the field?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:13.240
No, it's free. We can't.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.920
Let's try it again.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:18.360
Maybe we'll get drunk, and we'll even be able to drink a cup of vodka for the night.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:25.830
Of course. There's no point in staying in the field.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:08:00.000
- Thank you, Bull Hooter. - Don't lag behind, brother. You'll get a place to stay. - Yeah. - Get lost!

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:03.390
- What's wrong, master? - Who's there?

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.630
Don't offend the people! The Bible is free!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.030
- The philosopher Brut! - Rhetor Gorobets!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:13.060
I can't! My yard is full of people!

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:17.290
- Where am I going to put you? - In mercy, granny!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.890
How is it possible that Christian souls disappear for no reason?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.690
We won't be able to fit in there!

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.810
If we do something or do something else, then let us...

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.410
All right, I'll let you in.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.850
I'll put it all in the right places.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.150
It's your choice, we're not proud.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:54.280
What, granny, if, as they say...

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.590
In the stomach, like wheels, who began to eat?

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:59.090
In the morning, here would be a pinch in the mouth.

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.000
From what?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.060
They wanted to do anything, but my stove is not heated today.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.770
And we would pay for all this tomorrow as it should be, cleanly, huh?

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:14.440
Yes, damn it, I'll get something from this Kikimora.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.980
Come here, boy.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.900
Who? Me?

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.940
Me?

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.680
I'm in the house.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:42.000
And your place is long.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.180
To the sea.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:56.200
Granny!

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.510
Let's go.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.160
What is it, granny? What do you want?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:08.760
Listen, granny, it's fast now, and I'm such a person that I don't want to starve to death for a thousand gold coins.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.270
You're kidding, granny, I'm old.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.920
I'm with you, granny!

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:06.610
This is the witch!

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:11.210
Wicked witch!

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.780
Get down and retreat!

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.210
By the power of the Lord,

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.620
by the Lord God,

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.360
Jesus Christ, get down and retreat!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:24.250
I am protecting you!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.930
Christ is protecting you!

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.620
I am the Apostle of the Lamb!

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:14.950
Prys, you need to go to the doctor.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.820
You know how to go to the doctor.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:22.920
Hey, Khaman, what do you want?

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.660
Go to the rector, they've come with you.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:17:00.000
A few minutes later, the daughter of one of the richest houndstooth hunters,

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.600
She is in 50 versts away from Kiev.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.700
Yesterday she came back from a walk.

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:07.840
All beaten up, barely alive.

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:12.050
Before the death hour, she expressed a desire

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:16.410
that you, Hamak-Brut, read the departure letter on it.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:21.540
- Padre, I can't do that. - Come on, come on!

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:24.550
Without any excuses, get on the road!

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:28.520
The famous Sotnik sent a bunch of people to take care of you.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.000
What do you want to do with me?

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:31.330
Mr. Rector, I'm not going!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:35.790
Yes, no devil asks you whether you want to go or not.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:47.600
Thank you, sir. Call Yaitsev and tell him that as soon as the books he writes are ready, I will send them immediately.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:18:00.000
And I will only tell you that if you still show your moustache and be wise, then I will order you on your back and otherwise.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:05.530
You will have no need to go to the bathroom anymore.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:10.940
Go away with God, bow to the Lord.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:15.830
I'm in the spirit.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.760
Pour a pot of Gorilka for the good guys.

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:23.690
And what are you standing for?

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:24.960
With God!

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:30.000
Don't forget what I'm telling you!

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:37.330
Yes, the philosopher has to tie, not the one who is the one who takes it.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:42.480
Hello, brothers and comrades.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.280
Hello, Mr. Philosopher.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:48.760
So it's me, brothers and comrades, who have to sit with you.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:54.430
The factory is noble.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:58.360
Yes, the crew is of the same size.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.000
I would like to hire a musician.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:11.240
Then you can dance, ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:29.670
You know, for example, if we load this brick with some kind of product, let's say, salt,

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:31.480
Or with railway tracks.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.600
How many horses would be required?

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.280
Yes.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.560
Huh?

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:40.560
A sufficient number of horses would be required.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:44.700
And it's interesting, why is this lady so confused,

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.860
that it is necessary to read the departure notice on her?

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.560
Well, wait, Mr. Philosopher, why didn't you come?

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.860
Come on, guys, we're here!

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:48.960
Come on, Mr. Colossus, look, don't forget to drink.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.770
- Please, if you can, come in. - Do you have a gorilla?

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.640
Yes, yes, come in, please.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:16.800
To his guys, to the health of Mr. Rector!

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:18.950
Yes, Mr. Philosopher!

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:24.720
Guys, to the health of Mr. Rector!

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:25.320
Drink!

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:27.590
Drink, drink, gentlemen!

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:23.820
Does he think he is the only one who reads the church, or the other one?

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:34.040
I'll go to Bursa, too.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.340
I'll go to Yelbov.

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.160
Do you think I won't learn?

00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:41.660
I'll learn everything, everything.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:44.150
Oh, my God, my God, let it be.

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:52.780
The chumak sings, the chumak sings,

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.760
the chumak sings, the chumak sings,

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:05.030
- And I want to know... - Go to hell yourself, father.

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:11.920
Don't ask, don't ask. God knows how to do it. God knows everything.

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:16.920
No, I want to know what's written in those books.

00:24:16.920 --> 00:24:19.740
Oh, my God!

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:24.560
Oh, my God! What are you talking about?

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:28.390
Let me go! Why should I let you go?

00:24:28.390 --> 00:24:30.000
- Oh, my God!

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:41.900
What have you found?

00:24:49.820 --> 00:24:52.190
Let me go, brothers!

00:24:52.190 --> 00:24:55.990
Let me go!

00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:41.200
The lady is dead! The lady is dead! The lady is dead!

00:25:46.150 --> 00:25:48.480
The jar is dead!

00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:49.480
The jar is dead!

00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:51.340
Is it dead already?

00:26:01.080 --> 00:26:04.200
Sit down, Sirko, Anocha has died. Sit down!

00:26:09.060 --> 00:26:12.480
Let's let the hamster go home, brothers.

00:26:16.230 --> 00:26:20.390
Let's let it go, brothers, let it go on its own.

00:26:20.470 --> 00:26:22.150
Let it go on its own.

00:26:24.630 --> 00:26:30.000
- You're spitting on me! - You're spitting on me!

00:27:41.390 --> 00:27:44.950
Mr. Philosopher thinks he can get away from the village for nothing.

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:48.800
It's not the kind of place where you could get away.

00:27:49.670 --> 00:27:53.920
You'd better go to the master. He's waiting for you in the sanctuary.

00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:58.840
Well, I'd love to.

00:28:08.380 --> 00:28:13.300
I am sorry, my dearest daughter, that in 23 years, not even the supposed century,

00:28:13.300 --> 00:28:17.120
you left me the earth in sorrow and grief.

00:28:17.120 --> 00:28:26.370
I know who was my fierce enemy, the cause of your death.

00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:41.910
Who are you? And what rank do you have, kind man?

00:28:41.910 --> 00:28:45.360
I'm from the Bursak family. I'm a Home Abroad philosopher.

00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:54.160
- And who was your father? - I don't know, good man.

00:28:54.160 --> 00:28:58.740
- And who is your mother? - I don't know my mother either.

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:07.520
I did think about her, but I don't know who she was, where she came from or when she lived.

00:29:07.520 --> 00:29:11.810
How did you get to know my daughter?

00:29:11.810 --> 00:29:30.000
I didn't get to know her. I haven't had any business with her for as long as I've lived.

00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:35.160
- Not to mention the indecent. - Why did she begin to read to you and no one else?

00:29:36.020 --> 00:29:39.590
God knows how to interpret it.

00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:43.990
It's a well-known fact that we sometimes want something

00:29:44.190 --> 00:29:46.590
that even the most intelligent person can't understand.

00:29:46.790 --> 00:29:49.990
And the proverb says: "Run as fast as you can."

00:29:50.190 --> 00:29:52.190
Aren't you lying, Mr. Philosopher?

00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:56.150
At this very place. Let the thunder be so loud, if I come.

00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:17.830
If you gave me a minute, I would have returned everything.

00:30:17.830 --> 00:30:20.160
Don't let anyone read about me.

00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:23.140
But go to the Kiev Seminary at this hour

00:30:23.140 --> 00:30:27.400
and bring Bursak Khomubrut.

00:30:27.400 --> 00:30:30.000
Let him pray for three nights

00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:48.140
- Who knows? - I haven't heard about it yet.

00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:54.750
You are a good man, well-known for your holy life and godly deeds.

00:30:54.750 --> 00:31:00.000
- Maybe she heard about you? - Who, me?

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.300
God be with you, sir! What are you talking about?

00:31:03.540 --> 00:31:06.310
I, though it's unworthy of me to say,

00:31:06.750 --> 00:31:09.400
went to Bolshnitsa against the Rostov-on-Don fours.

00:31:09.680 --> 00:31:17.450
Well, it's not for nothing that you're appointed like this.

00:31:17.730 --> 00:31:22.350
You have to start your own business from today.

00:31:23.510 --> 00:31:26.130
I would say, at your mercy.

00:31:26.450 --> 00:31:30.000
Well, of course, every person has a reason to do so.

00:31:30.060 --> 00:31:32.980
the Holy Scripture may be of a large scale.

00:31:33.040 --> 00:31:38.360
Only a deacon or at least a deacon would be more appropriate here.

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:43.820
They are a people of knowledge and will do everything as it should be done.

00:31:44.020 --> 00:31:46.800
And I have such a voice, too, and I myself...

00:31:46.980 --> 00:31:49.440
God knows what! I don't have any kind of a voice.

00:31:49.600 --> 00:31:54.220
As you know, only I will fulfill all that my beloved has promised me.

00:31:54.320 --> 00:31:56.350
I will not regret anything.

00:31:56.440 --> 00:32:00.000
And if you, from the same day, at three o'clock in the morning,

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:07.650
If you perform a prayer on it, I'll reward you, and if you don't,

00:34:38.670 --> 00:34:48.920
Forgive the deceased for the first time, forgive the deceased for the second time, forgive the deceased for the third time.

00:36:17.690 --> 00:36:21.250
to feed the philosophers and take them to church after dinner.

00:36:31.920 --> 00:36:35.400
It's a pity, Mr. Philosopher, you didn't know Mikitka.

00:36:35.400 --> 00:36:37.790
He was a rare man.

00:36:37.790 --> 00:36:41.970
Everyone knows the dog as well as their own father.

00:36:41.970 --> 00:36:44.700
The dog was a great man.

00:36:44.700 --> 00:36:53.240
But after a while he began to look endlessly at Pannochka.

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:58.200
Was he glancing at her or was she bewitching him?

00:36:58.200 --> 00:37:00.000
The man disappeared.

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:06.080
One time the gentleman came to the stable where he was cleaning the horse

00:37:06.080 --> 00:37:10.080
and said, "Give me a stick, I'll put my foot on you."

00:37:10.080 --> 00:37:13.900
And he, poor fellow, was happy about it and said,

00:37:13.900 --> 00:37:17.820
"Not only the foot, but also sit on me yourself."

00:37:17.820 --> 00:37:23.540
And he, a fool, bent his back and went to jump.

00:37:23.540 --> 00:37:30.000
Well, gentlemen, it's time for us to see the philosopher.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.220
I want to go to the cemetery.

00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:25.560
- Well, boy, be healthy. - May it be good for you.

00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:30.000
- Good luck with your business. - I'm sorry, but we'll lock you up.

00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:35.630
- We carry out the master's order. - It's okay, I'll work it out somehow.

00:38:35.630 --> 00:38:41.970
But the master will give me both pockets with pure reds.

00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:29.800
- He will be afraid of God's word. - Right, right.

00:39:31.050 --> 00:39:36.150
- Let him lie down. - What are you talking about, Cossack?

00:39:36.150 --> 00:39:44.030
When would you be afraid? A man can't come here.

00:39:44.030 --> 00:39:48.840
And I have prayers from the dead and those who come out of that world.

00:39:48.840 --> 00:39:54.610
And when I read them, they won't touch me with a finger.

00:39:54.610 --> 00:39:57.140
Nothing. Thank God they won't touch me.

00:40:10.080 --> 00:40:13.900
- What are you afraid of? - I drank too much.

00:40:13.900 --> 00:40:20.520
- It seems scary. - Candles.

00:40:20.520 --> 00:40:30.000
- That's good. We need to illuminate the church.

00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:38.320
So that you can see how it is during the day.

00:41:06.520 --> 00:41:12.870
Nothing. I'll read it three nights in advance.

00:41:12.870 --> 00:41:20.040
The church must be lit in such a way that it can be seen as in the daytime.

00:41:20.040 --> 00:41:26.760
What to be afraid of? Fingers do not touch.

00:41:48.330 --> 00:41:58.390
Forgive me, Lord, how to read in the day?

00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:09.060
Blessed are those who walk in the way of the law,

00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:11.550
blessed are those who test His commandments,

00:42:11.550 --> 00:42:14.610
those who seek Him with all their heart.

00:42:14.610 --> 00:42:20.030
It's a pity that in the temple of God you can't smoke a cigarette.

00:42:20.030 --> 00:42:22.900
You walk in the way of the law that doesn't do anything wrong.

00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:29.220
You have promised to eat your commandments and to smell tobacco.

00:42:31.880 --> 00:42:38.930
Good tobacco, glorious tobacco, good tobacco.

00:43:01.080 --> 00:43:30.000
Oh my God, Bavaria, save the church, my God, my God, save the church.

00:43:30.830 --> 00:43:33.450
Save me. Save the church.

00:43:36.810 --> 00:43:38.260
Die, die.

00:43:40.760 --> 00:43:44.880
In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.

00:43:44.960 --> 00:43:45.910
In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.

00:44:00.510 --> 00:44:03.300
I won't hear a word from her again.

00:46:23.960 --> 00:46:24.740
Look, philosopher.

00:46:35.790 --> 00:46:37.590
Oh, what a wonderful place!

00:46:38.890 --> 00:46:54.900
I'd like to live here and catch some fish and go to the yard.

00:46:55.470 --> 00:47:00.000
- I'd like to sleep here. - You can't, philosopher, it's not allowed.

00:47:10.910 --> 00:47:13.380
Well, girls, have you cooked borscht?

00:47:13.380 --> 00:47:15.630
Yes, we have, uncle, we have.

00:47:15.630 --> 00:47:17.640
It must be tasty, huh?

00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:20.130
I'll ask the philosopher.

00:47:43.280 --> 00:48:00.000
- How? - What happened?

00:48:02.080 --> 00:48:02.790
This is it.

00:48:42.410 --> 00:49:00.000
I'm sorry, the girl is already wet from the skin behind me.

00:49:05.370 --> 00:49:11.240
Drink some water and you'll forget your girlfriend

00:49:12.370 --> 00:49:18.920
I drank water, I drank cold water, but I don't forget

00:49:19.150 --> 00:49:25.760
Until I'm alive, I won't forget who I love

00:49:28.670 --> 00:49:29.380
Well

00:49:38.760 --> 00:49:43.650
A Cossack should not be afraid of anything in this world.

00:49:51.620 --> 00:49:53.620
Let's go to the plow!

00:50:45.420 --> 00:50:48.310
A Cossack shouldn't be afraid of anything.

00:50:48.310 --> 00:51:00.000
It's scary the first time, but then it's not scary anymore.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:04.480
It's not scary anymore, it's not scary at all.

00:51:04.480 --> 00:51:30.000
It's not scary anymore, no one touches it, not even your rage.

00:51:30.060 --> 00:51:36.020
You will heal me, and I will not be punished by Your wrath.

00:51:36.140 --> 00:51:43.580
Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I have no power.

00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:52.400
Heal me, O Lord, for my bones have been broken.

00:51:52.520 --> 00:51:55.260
My bones have been broken.

00:51:55.380 --> 00:52:00.000
Let not the water-storm drown me, let not the fire burn me.

00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:02.240
Yes, I am a witness.

00:52:03.560 --> 00:52:04.910
God, save me.

00:52:04.910 --> 00:52:06.230
God, save me.

00:52:06.230 --> 00:52:07.240
God, save me.

00:52:07.240 --> 00:52:08.140
God, save me.

00:52:10.820 --> 00:52:13.320
God, I bear your horror again.

00:52:14.200 --> 00:52:17.200
God, again I bear your horror.

00:52:17.200 --> 00:52:18.700
I don't give up.

00:52:18.700 --> 00:52:20.650
Yes, God, God!

00:52:20.650 --> 00:52:23.740
You, God, are alive!

00:52:23.740 --> 00:52:26.500
Who killed you?

00:52:26.500 --> 00:52:27.640
Help me, God.

00:52:27.640 --> 00:52:29.050
Save my soul.

00:52:29.050 --> 00:52:30.000
Save me.

00:53:00.700 --> 00:53:02.600
*music*

00:54:00.410 --> 00:54:11.910
Let the blindness fall upon him, let the grayness be cast upon him, let the white snow be covered with it.

00:54:49.200 --> 00:54:49.810
Thank you.

00:56:32.200 --> 00:56:35.920
That's how long a person dances.

00:56:35.920 --> 00:56:39.520
Yes, long enough.

00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:42.360
Hey, philosopher, what's wrong with you?

00:56:42.360 --> 00:56:44.860
Don't you see, the silly woman is dancing.

00:56:44.860 --> 00:56:51.120
Oh, Lyshenko, but you sat all the time.

00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:56.880
You really sat, like our Sari Yavtukha.

00:57:00.320 --> 00:57:08.640
I'll go to the master and explain everything. I don't want to read anymore.

00:57:31.020 --> 00:57:36.010
- Is everything okay? - Yes, everything is okay.

00:57:37.030 --> 00:57:41.580
There's such a thing as "take a hat and lick it".

00:57:42.020 --> 00:57:46.070
- What do you mean? - Your lady is a daughter.

00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:52.050
She's of the noble kind, no one will touch her.

00:57:53.080 --> 00:57:56.120
But not in anger, but in peace of God and her soul.

00:57:56.360 --> 00:58:00.000
- What, daughter? - Let her go.

00:58:06.520 --> 00:58:09.780
I didn't call you for nothing.

00:58:09.780 --> 00:58:12.680
She took care of saving her soul.

00:58:12.680 --> 00:58:18.150
And she wanted to expel all bad thoughts with prayers.

00:58:18.150 --> 00:58:21.800
Your Lordship, God forbid!

00:58:21.800 --> 00:58:26.860
Read, read. You have only one night left.

00:58:26.860 --> 00:58:30.000
You will do a divine deed, and I will reward you.

00:58:33.390 --> 00:58:43.560
No matter what reward it is, I will not read it, as you wish, sir.

00:58:43.560 --> 00:58:58.680
Listen to these ideas. You can do it in your bursa.

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:06.680
I'm not like that. I'm not your rector anymore.

00:59:06.990 --> 00:59:12.150
Do you know what good leather hooks are?

00:59:12.350 --> 00:59:17.120
How can I not know? Everyone knows what leather hooks are.

00:59:17.280 --> 00:59:19.800
It's an unbearable thing.

00:59:19.940 --> 00:59:23.320
You're right, you don't know how my lads know how to steam.

00:59:23.490 --> 00:59:30.000
They'll steam first, then they'll spray the burner,

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:42.960
And then do your job again.

00:59:42.960 --> 00:59:49.090
If you don't do it, you won't get up.

00:59:49.090 --> 00:59:54.640
And if you do, you'll get a thousand reds.

01:01:03.230 --> 01:01:10.690
I'm going to make a new one.

01:01:31.080 --> 01:01:43.890
You are still red, probably the old skryaga is lying, but yes, nothing, Mr. Hundred, I'm so excited that you and your dogs will not chase me away.

01:02:23.260 --> 01:02:28.450
Such a hook! And I feel sorry for Sertuk.

01:02:33.290 --> 01:02:37.810
The dress is nice. Why did you pay for it?

01:02:37.810 --> 01:02:48.600
It suits you, Uncle Yevtukh.

01:03:10.110 --> 01:03:10.630
Yes.

01:03:59.150 --> 01:03:59.830
What do you want?

01:04:00.800 --> 01:04:15.240
Then go to church, Ossoff, are you afraid?

01:04:15.240 --> 01:04:19.760
Well, now the witch will give it to you, and I'll take it.

01:04:19.760 --> 01:04:23.010
What am I afraid of? Am I not a Cossack?

01:04:23.010 --> 01:04:28.040
I read "Two Nights", "God and the Three Kings" will help.

01:04:32.840 --> 01:04:39.060
It seems that the damned witch has made a decent amount of sins that the evil forces are standing for her.

01:04:39.060 --> 01:04:57.880
Mr. Philosopher, it's time to go to the church. Come on, let's go.

01:05:07.800 --> 01:05:30.000
- For you, sir. - It's his fate. - He'll get away, sir!

01:05:30.920 --> 01:05:36.790
- You're still red. - I'm going for a walk, uncle Evtukh.

01:05:36.790 --> 01:05:44.050
- Go read. - Go read, philosopher.

01:06:09.340 --> 01:06:10.310
Oops!

01:06:57.640 --> 01:07:00.000
Oh, my God!

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:06.320
And in madness and in madness I am a beggar.

01:07:06.320 --> 01:07:13.840
And in the works of my youth, I can not leave you.

01:07:13.840 --> 01:07:19.590
God, help me, my helper, my deliverer.

01:07:19.590 --> 01:07:21.270
Seek, O Lord, do not bite.

01:07:21.270 --> 01:07:30.000
Whether you create miracles by the dead, or the doctors will resurrect the confession,

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:48.190
They will hide in the village, they will keep my drink, how can you bear my soul? Who will tell you? Worked with my breath.

01:08:03.420 --> 01:08:05.560
I will touch you!

01:08:05.560 --> 01:08:08.570
I will curse you with my tail!

01:08:08.570 --> 01:08:10.710
With my dog tail!

01:08:10.710 --> 01:08:16.830
With my ax!

01:08:16.830 --> 01:08:18.850
I will curse you!

01:08:18.850 --> 01:08:21.540
I will curse you!

01:08:21.540 --> 01:08:25.440
I will curse you!

01:09:01.790 --> 01:09:04.550
Come to me, burdolaki!

01:09:31.370 --> 01:09:34.100
I don't know what I'm doing here!

01:10:50.920 --> 01:10:52.320
Find him!

01:10:52.320 --> 01:10:54.470
Find him!

01:10:54.470 --> 01:10:57.230
Find him!

01:10:57.230 --> 01:11:00.000
Give me back my eyelids!

01:11:01.950 --> 01:11:04.200
- I'm sorry!

01:11:31.530 --> 01:11:35.160
I'm not a Muslim!

01:13:02.560 --> 01:13:06.210
Yes, our Khoma is not lucky.

01:13:06.210 --> 01:13:08.850
So God gave him.

01:13:08.850 --> 01:13:11.620
Let's remember his soul.

01:13:11.620 --> 01:13:30.000
Heh, Khoma was a noble man, he was a noble man.

01:13:35.120 --> 01:13:38.070
- But he didn't disappear for what? - I know why he disappeared.

01:13:38.070 --> 01:13:40.310
- Why? - Because he got scared.

01:13:40.310 --> 01:13:44.000
And if he hadn't got scared, the witch wouldn't have been able to do anything to him.

01:13:44.000 --> 01:13:49.620
All he had to do was cross his hands and spit on his tail, and nothing would have happened.

01:13:49.620 --> 01:13:52.440
I know all that.

01:13:52.440 --> 01:13:56.970
In Kyiv, all the women who sit on the bazaar are witches.

01:13:56.970 --> 01:13:59.920
He got scared, and that's why he disappeared.

01:14:02.460 --> 01:14:07.550
- Who saw him disappear? - They say so.

01:14:08.460 --> 01:14:11.380
They say so, if it's all a lie.

01:14:11.970 --> 01:14:14.790
And that he disappeared, and about the witch too.

01:14:15.990 --> 01:14:19.600
He didn't seem like that to me after the third step.

01:14:26.830 --> 01:14:28.900
Or maybe he didn't die at all.

01:14:32.490 --> 01:14:35.810
Maybe he's coming here. See?

01:14:41.970 --> 01:14:54.860
- What do you mean "he"? - You're working.

01:14:55.570 --> 01:15:00.000
- Working? - Yes, working.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:00.740
Take a break.
